==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
After {{w|King Solomon}}, whose mines of immense wealth {{w|Álvaro de Mendaña y Neira}} hoped to find when he named it in 1567 or 1568.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|AU}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɒləmən ˈaɪləndz/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɒl.ə.mən ˈaɪ.ləndz/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɑ.lə.mən ˈaɪ.ləndz/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Solomon Islands.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[Solomon]] [[island|Islands]]}}

# {{senseid|en|Q685}}{{place|en|country|r/Melanesia}}.
# An archipelago including most of the country of the Solomon Islands (though excluding the Santa Cruz Islands) and the island of [[Bougainville]].

====Holonyms====
* {{l|en|Melanesia}}

